## Exact-head law

Every CI claim is indexed as `CI(repository, SHA)`. Branch names, PR numbers, workflow names,
and older green runs do not transfer standing to a newer head. Re-observe the PR head, run head,
job/step evidence, artifact identities, and consequence before assigning `ALIVE`.

## BLOCKED law

`BLOCKED` is admissible only after all relevant lawful connector, Actions, artifact,
materialization, authority, and compatible-execution routes are attempted or eliminated with
typed evidence. If a route remains `AVAILABLE` or `CANDIDATE`, the pack's topology gate refuses
`BLOCKED`.

## BRCE-shaped publication law

SELECT, CONSTRUCT, and DO remain distinct. Generated graphs, plans, hooks, and workflow
definitions have no ambient actuation authority. Consequential operations require explicit
authority and receipt closure. Publication defaults to purpose branch + intentional commit +
draft PR; merge/close requires separate authority.
